(10.7 Exact SQLAlchemy And Pydantic Type Direction) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This section is important for a fresher developer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It clearly says which backend type to use.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SQLAlchemy Type Mapping) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use these standard mappings:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `id`: `Mapped[int]` with `BigInteger` or `Integer`) Tj
T*
(- text name fields: `Mapped[str]` with `String\(length\)`) Tj
T*
(- long notes: `Mapped[str | None]` with `Text`) Tj
T*
(- flags: `Mapped[bool]` with `Boolean`) Tj
T*
(- decimal hours: `Mapped[Decimal]` or `Mapped[float]` with `Numeric\(10, 2\)`) Tj
T*
(- timestamps: `Mapped[datetime]` with `DateTime\(timezone=True\)`) Tj
T*
(- pure dates: `Mapped[date]` with `Date`) Tj
T*
(- pure time values: `Mapped[time | None]` with `Time`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pydantic Field Type Mapping) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use these field types in request and response schemas:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `id`: `int`) Tj
T*
(- `name`: `str`) Tj
T*
(- `description`: `str | None`) Tj
T*
(- `is_active`: `bool`) Tj
T*
(- `date`: `date`) Tj
T*
(- `timestamp`: `datetime`) Tj
T*
(- `requested_hours`: `float`) Tj
T*
(- `approved_hours`: `float | None`) Tj
T*
(- arrays: `list[SomeSchema]`) Tj
T*
(- string maps: `dict[str, list[str]]`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Enum Values To Standardize) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Do not allow free text everywhere.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use fixed values like:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `request_type`: `'timeoff' | 'regularization'`) Tj
T*
(- `status`: `'pending' | 'approved' | 'rejected' | 'cancelled'`) Tj
T*
(- `duration_type`: `'full_day' | 'half_day' | 'hourly'`) Tj
T*
(- `assigned_role`: `'hr' | 'admin'`) Tj
T*
(- `employment_status`: `'active' | 'inactive' | 'notice_period' | 'relieved'`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10.8 Suggested Pydantic Schemas) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
